# Local Performance Reviewer

Use the local Ollama + SQLite RAG agent (not Cursor Cloud) to detect performance concerns:

```bash
./scripts/pr-review-index.sh   # shared RAG index (with PR reviewer)
./scripts/perf-review.sh       # current branch
./scripts/perf-review.sh --pr 42
```

Rules: `agents/performance-reviewer/RULES.md`.
Index: `agents/pr-reviewer/index/rag.sqlite` (shared).

Focus on:

- Rebuild waste (`BlocBuilder` without `buildWhen`, broad `setState`)
- Lists / scroll (`ListView(children:)` vs builders, `shrinkWrap`, nested scrollables)
- Images (`Image.network` without cache size hints)
- Main-isolate stalls (sync JSON/file work on UI/bloc paths)
- Layout/animation cost (`Opacity` for fades)

Keep findings actionable and file-scoped. Prefer evidence from the diff, nearby hunks, prechecks, and RAG — not generic Flutter advice.
